{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And he smelled the smell of his garments.</b> To expand his soul through the delights of fragrance, as the Sages of blessed memory said (Berakhot 43b): What is a thing from which the soul derives pleasure but the body does not? Say: this is fragrance." "<b>And he blessed him.</b> As in וְהָיָה כְּנַגֵּן הַמְנַגֵּן וַתְּהִי עָלָיו יַד ה' (II Kings 3:15)." "<b>See, the smell of my son.</b> You are my son — see and consider that this fragrance is" "<b>As the smell of a field.</b> For besides its sufficiency to serve as sustenance for living creatures, He added to it the excellence of fragrance, which gives pleasure and benefit to the vital spirit and the soul. And this is of the ways of His goodness." "<b>Which YHWH has blessed. And may the Elohim give you.</b> And upon your contemplating the measure of His goodness, He will give you, in that He is the Elohim, a blessed field."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:32:01.935237027Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}